Muse Pocket changes add X4 Pro display/controls, preserved-image recovery,
local private token packaging, generic companion initialization and public docs.
Modified inherited source files carry a Muse Pocket modification notice.
New Muse Pocket source, docs and neutral placeholder art use Apache-2.0.
The upstream license-excluded Jollybot art is omitted and replaced with original
neutral display icons. The retained SDK's other board profiles are not qualified
as Muse Pocket products.

esp32/components/xteink_epd contains a pinned MIT subset of FreeInk:
https://github.com/Free-Ink/freeink-sdk
Commit: 6af90c4c50b4e067516bb4c344bb686a26f1da52
See that directory's LICENSE and UPSTREAM.md for attribution and modifications.

esp32/main/pixel_font.c retains the Adafruit BSD-2-Clause notice in its header.
esp32/components/minimp3/include/minimp3.h retains CC0-1.0; see its LICENSE.
Dependencies fetched by ESP-IDF keep their own licenses.

esp32/dev_signing_key.pem is the deliberately public SDK DEVELOPMENT test key,
unchanged from the upstream snapshot (SHA256 e57311281ea0478a80be57036768ef71481804eab73182b2b70255311a2ded6a).
It is not a user's secret or a production signing identity. Do not use it to
secure hardware. Muse Pocket's X4 Pro profile does not enable secure boot.

Muse service access and pairing are also subject to the Gadget SDK Terms:
https://gadgets.muse.ai/sdk-terms
